cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the paper it accompanies (see preferred-citation below)."
title: "reservoirpressure-uq"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Eze"
    given-names: "Gabriel Nwachuku"
    affiliation: "King Fahd University of Petroleum & Minerals"
abstract: >
  Non-intrusive polynomial chaos expansion (PCE) on a Smolyak sparse grid for
  real-time uncertainty quantification of average reservoir pressure estimates,
  validated against a digital twin of Volve well 15/9-F-14 H and applied to the
  real 3,056-day production record, with a drawdown-weighted Bayesian
  model-averaging layer reconciling productivity-index and material-balance
  model-form divergence.
keywords:
  - reservoir pressure estimation
  - uncertainty quantification
  - polynomial chaos expansion
  - Smolyak sparse grid
  - Sobol' sensitivity analysis
  - Bayesian model averaging
  - digital twin
  - smart wells
